  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The political discourse surrounding the selection of a new Vice President has intensified following reports regarding the potential replacement of Gibran Rakabuming Raka. Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, who currently serves as the Deputy Speaker of the House of Representatives and as the Executive Chairman of the Gerindra Party, has received support from various stakeholders, including academic leaders and religious figures. Observers suggest that these endorsements are based on his perceived skills as a consolidator and his potential market acceptance. Meanwhile, some analysts suggest that outside groups are intentionally generating negative sentiment against the candidate to influence the selection process. Officials have noted that if legislative efforts to appoint a successor remain deadlocked, President Prabowo Subianto may be required to intervene to finalize the appointment. The ongoing discussions reflect broader strategic considerations for the administration's political future ahead of the 2029 cycle.",
